  #line-at(90.024pt, 84.14pt, "coincide with the aforementioned principle of constructing liquid metal micro-units ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 99.74pt, "rather than deliberately mimicking the structure of the cell just for the sake of ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 115.34pt, "biomimicry. ")
  #line-at(114.02pt, 130.94pt, "Based on these correlations between liquid metals and living cells, this study ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 146.54pt, "proposes the concept of biomimetic liquid metal cells (LMCs). As the fundamental ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 162.14pt, "structural and functional units of liquid metal living matter, it is an extensible and ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 177.74pt, "multifunctional platform that fully exploits the comprehensive properties of liquid ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 193.34pt, "metals, possessing the potential for bottom-up assembly into more complex functional ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 208.94pt, "entities and even systems. First, we elaborate on the structural design, material ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 224.54pt, "composition, and fabrication protocol of LMCs. Then, we explore the response of ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 240.17pt, "LMCs under various physical and chemical fields and disclose that LMCs have natural ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 255.77pt, "sensing functions and respond immediately to environmental changes. In addition, ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 271.37pt, "LMCs can also actively exhibit electrophilic and magnetotropic behaviors followed by ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 286.97pt, "directional movements. Finally, as an illustrative example, we demonstrate the potential ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 302.57pt, "application of LMCs as sensors, fluidic valves, and material transport carriers in a ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 318.17pt, "converging channel. The LMCs developed here significantly expand the current ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 333.77pt, "understanding of liquid metals while offering new possibilities for constructing more ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 349.37pt, "sophisticated liquid metal living matters, paving a promising way in making the ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 364.97pt, "artificial life system from bottom up. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 14.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.024pt, 404.95pt, "2. Materials and Methods ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.024pt, 431.47pt, "2.1 Materials ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(114.02pt, 450.79pt, "Unless otherwise stated, all liquid metal mentioned in this study refers to pure ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 466.39pt, "EGaIn. EGaIn is prepared by mixing 75.5 wt% gallium and 24.5 wt% indium, and ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 481.99pt, "melting the mixture in a vacuum oven at 150°C for 6 hours. ")
  #line-at(114.02pt, 497.59pt, "Sodium alginate (90%) and calcium lactate hydrate (C6H10CaO6·xH2O, 98wt%) ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 513.19pt, "were purchased from Shanghai Macklin Biochemical Technology CO., Ltd. ")
  #line-at(114.02pt, 528.79pt, "Poly (3,4-ethylenedioxythiophene)-poly (styrene sulfonate) (PEDOT: PSS, 1.1% ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 544.39pt, "concentration in H₂O, without surfactants, and exhibiting high conductivity) was ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 559.99pt, "purchased from Shanghai Aladdin Biochemical Technology CO., Ltd.  ")
  #line-at(114.02pt, 575.62pt, "Iron nanoparticles (99.9% metals basis, 100 nm average particle size) were ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 591.22pt, "purchased from Shanghai Macklin Biochemical Technology Co., Ltd. ")
  #line-at(114.02pt, 606.82pt, "Deionized water used for solution preparation was obtained from a ultrapure water ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 622.42pt, "system (Direct-Q 3 UV, Merck Millipore, Germany).")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.024pt, 642.1pt, "2.2 Preparation of SA-PEDOT: PSS composite gel solution ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(114.02pt, 661.42pt, "Dilute the PEDOT: PSS solution, and then add Sodium alginate (SA) powder to ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 677.02pt, "the mixture. After manual stirring until homogeneous, degas the solution under a ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 692.62pt, "vacuum. The final concentrations are 0.033 wt% PEDOT: PSS and 1.5 wt% SA. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.024pt, 716.26pt, "2.3 Details and procedural steps of the layered cryogenic molding method ")
  #line-at(114.14pt, 739.56pt, "Step 1")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(147.14pt, 739.56pt, ": Fill the target Ecoflex mold halfway with a 0.5 mol/L NaOH solution, ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 755.04pt, "lightly shake to remove bubbles, and freeze at -8 °C for 6 hours until the solution is ")
]

