  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 14.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.024pt, 170.9pt, "4. Versatile Responses of LMCs under External Fields ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(114.02pt, 193.34pt, "Timely response to unknown changes and risks is fundamental for life systems to ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 208.94pt, "achieve survival, adaptation, and evolution. As a system parallel to the natural life ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 224.54pt, "system, the liquid metal living matter system must also confront complex and dynamic ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 240.17pt, "environments, rather than being perpetually protected within ideal laboratory ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 255.77pt, "conditions. As the foundation for establishing this artificial system, LMCs facilitate the ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 271.37pt, "transition of liquid metal from dependency on solution environments to functioning as ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 286.97pt, "independent entities in open-air conditions, thereby directly addressing challenges. ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 302.57pt, "Furthermore, the proportion of liquid metal serving as the core component represents a ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 318.17pt, "critical design parameter that fundamentally influences the properties and functions of ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 333.77pt, "LMCs. Therefore, we have systematically investigated the impact of liquid metal core ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 349.49pt, "content on LMC behavior (")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(223.01pt, 349.49pt, "Fig. 2A")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(260.69pt, 349.49pt, "). This section selects three representative external ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 364.97pt, "stimulus—temperature, pressure, and chemical fields—to explore how these cells adapt ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 380.69pt, "to natural environments (")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(215.69pt, 380.69pt, "Fig. 2B")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(253.85pt, 380.69pt, "). To effectively capture the dynamic responses of ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 396.17pt, "LMCs, we utilize electrical resistance as a key parameter, given that the constituent ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 411.79pt, "elements of the LMCs are all electrically conductive. It serves as a sensitive and ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 427.39pt, "quantifiable indicator of the structural and compositional changes within the cells when ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 442.99pt, "exposed to external stimuli. We discover that LMCs possess an inherent sensing ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 458.59pt, "capability. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.024pt, 482.23pt, "4.1 Thermal response ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(114.02pt, 505.39pt, "Temperature fluctuations are inevitable in practical operational environments. To ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 520.99pt, "further investigate their behavior under varying thermal conditions, LMCs are ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 536.59pt, "maintained under controlled isothermal conditions across different temperature regimes ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 552.19pt, "from 15 °C to 40 °C. By real-time monitoring of the average temperature at three points ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 567.82pt, "(top, middle, and bottom) and longitudinal resistance, we explore the impact of both ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 583.42pt, "internal liquid metal content and external temperature variations on the overall ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 599.02pt, "electrical properties of LMCs. Due to the high conductivity of liquid metal, the LMCs ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 614.62pt, "exhibit significantly lower resistance compared to the equal-volume hydrogel vesicles ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 630.22pt, "containing only solution. The resistance of LMCs exhibits an inverse relationship with ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 645.94pt, "temperature elevation (")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(204.05pt, 645.94pt, "Fig. 2C")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(242.69pt, 645.94pt, "). To analyze this phenomenon, we first examine the ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 661.42pt, "thermal effects on the conductivity of individual components. With increasing ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 677.02pt, "temperature, liquid metals show decreased electrical conductivity (")
