#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(293.21pt, 778.08pt, "14 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.024pt, 84.26pt, "3C)")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(108.62pt, 84.26pt, ". The magnetic LMCs exhibit distinct locomotion characteristics with remarkable ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 99.74pt, "multi-dimensional mobility, including lateral movement, anti-gravity motion, and ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 115.34pt, "corner-crossing motion guided by a NdFeB magnet. The sequential motion trajectory ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 130.94pt, "(positions i-iii) illustrates one-dimensional lateral movement confined to a horizontal ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 146.54pt, "platform. The liquid metal core preserves high surface tension and maintains at the ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 162.26pt, "bottom because of gravitational effects (")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(291.77pt, 162.26pt, "Fig. 3D")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(330.67pt, 162.74pt, "1")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(334.75pt, 162.26pt, "). When the magnetic force in the ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 177.74pt, "vertical direction counterbalances the gravitational force, the LMC achieves controlled ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 193.34pt, "suspension. Sequential motion trajectory (positions iv-viii) shows the flexible two-")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 208.94pt, "dimensional motion of the magnetic LMC under the guidance of the magnet. It enters ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 224.54pt, "a suspended state, with the liquid metal core stabilized centrally within the cell's inner ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 240.29pt, "membrane to the vertical wall (")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(251.09pt, 240.29pt, "Fig. 3D")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(290.45pt, 240.77pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(294.53pt, 240.29pt, "). This multidimensional manipulation via ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 255.77pt, "magnetic fields demonstrates that LMCs possess significant potential for functional ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 271.37pt, "evolution through strategic materials integration. Such capability facilitates the ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 286.97pt, "development of responsive systems capable of controlled directional movement under ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 302.57pt, "the tuning of various external fields including light, sound, thermal fields, etc. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 14.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.024pt, 340.97pt, "6. Capability of Resisting Low-Temperature Conditions  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(114.02pt, 371.21pt, "While the previous section examined LMC behavior under moderate temperature ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 386.81pt, "variations (15-40°C), extreme thermal conditions present more significant challenges ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 402.41pt, "for functional materials. Understanding the stability and performance retention of ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 418.03pt, "LMCs under extreme low-temperature conditions is crucial for evaluating their ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 433.63pt, "operational reliability across extended environmental ranges. Here, we explore their ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 449.23pt, "response to rapid cooling from above 0°C to -13°C, focusing on the property changes ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 464.83pt, "of both integral and individual components. Due to the high water content (95.39%)")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 480.43pt, "and the permeability of the hydrogel membrane, it is considered as a unified system ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 496.03pt, "with the solution, and both exhibit synchronized phase transitions. ")
  #line-at(114.02pt, 511.63pt, "To evaluate the effect of liquid metal on cold resistance, this section compares ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 527.23pt, "LMCs with pure vesicles of the same size containing only solution as a control. The ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 542.83pt, "control group exhibits distinct thermal behavior characterized by a temperature plateau ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 558.43pt, "at -5°C, with resistance changes showing a negative correlation with temperature ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 574.18pt, "variations before and after this point (")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(269.21pt, 574.18pt, "Fig. 4A")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(306.05pt, 574.18pt, "). In stage i, the hydrogel maintains its gel ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 589.66pt, "state while the solution remains liquid. A significant 103.143% step increase in ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 605.26pt, "resistance marked the phase transition between two distinct stages. Then, both ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 620.86pt, "components solidify in stage ii. ")
  #line-at(114.02pt, 636.58pt, "In contrast, LMCs demonstrate a more complex cooling process (")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(425.47pt, 636.58pt, "Fig. 4B")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(461.74pt, 636.58pt, "). During ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 652.06pt, "stage iii, resistance increases with decreasing temperature while maintaining the cell ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 667.66pt, "membrane's gel state and liquid phases of both solution and liquid metal. The cooling ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 683.26pt, "rates remain similar through stages i and iii due to the low volume fraction of liquid ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 698.86pt, "metal within the LMCs (10.234%) and extensive cooling source. Similarly, there is no ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 714.46pt, "significant influence on the phase transition time of the outer components. A 98.439% ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 730.06pt, "step increase in resistance marks the transition to stage iv, where all components except ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 745.68pt, "liquid metal solidified. ")
]

