  #line-at(293.21pt, 778.08pt, "18 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 14.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.024pt, 92.9pt, "8. Conclusion ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(114.02pt, 115.34pt, "In this study, we systematically present the concept, preliminary theory, and ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 130.94pt, "technology of LMCs as the fundamental structural and functional units of liquid metal ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 146.54pt, "living matter and successfully establish their fundamental architecture using a ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 162.14pt, "systematic bottom-up fabrication strategy. Through the layered cryogenic molding ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 177.74pt, "method, we develop a multi-layer and multi-phase cell mimic wherein the liquid metal ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 193.34pt, "core is the nucleus for responsive functionality. The reducing electrolyte solution works ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 208.94pt, "as the cytoplasm, simultaneously maintaining the metallic core's reductive state ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 224.54pt, "advantages while facilitating information and material exchange between the internal ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 240.17pt, "and external compartments. The outer membrane is an alginate-based composite ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 255.77pt, "hydrogel with a porous architecture, providing structural support and permeability for ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 271.37pt, "molecular and ionic transport. This LMC unit with a tri-layer architecture effectively ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 286.97pt, "addresses previous limitations of liquid metal applications in scale and environment, ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 302.57pt, "maintaining the morphological and physicochemical stability of liquid metals.  ")
  #line-at(114.02pt, 318.17pt, "As the basic unit of liquid metal living matter, the response properties of such ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 333.77pt, "LMCs to environmental stimuli are first investigated. Through systematic measurement ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 349.37pt, "and analysis of characteristic resistance, we find that LMCs possess remarkable sensing ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 364.97pt, "capabilities and environmental adaptability. They exhibit instantaneous and well-")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 380.57pt, "regulated resistance changes in response to varying temperature, pressure, and chemical ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 396.17pt, "fields. To clarify the response mechanisms induced by different environmental stimuli, ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 411.79pt, "we establish a geometric resistance model that links electrical resistance to the ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 427.39pt, "structural deformation of the LMC. Both experiment results and the resistance model ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 442.99pt, "demonstrate that the integration of the liquid metal core into the LMC structure ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 458.59pt, "significantly enhances its perceptual ability and intrinsic homeostasis, with the model ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 474.19pt, "successfully capturing the key scaling behaviors observed across different compression ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 489.79pt, "states.  ")
  #line-at(114.02pt, 505.39pt, "The multi-field tuning capability of LMCs builds the foundation for developing ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 520.99pt, "various external field responsive behaviors, the most typical of which are electrical and ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 536.59pt, "magnetic tuning behavior. Therefore, the movement controllability of LMCs under ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 552.19pt, "electric and magnetic fields is studied with varying liquid metal nuclei proportions. It ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 567.82pt, "reveals that LMCs are capable of controlled directional movement under electric fields, ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 583.42pt, "and LMCs with higher liquid metal adding ratios show more sensitive tuning ability, ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 599.02pt, "manifested by higher moving speed and lower activation voltage. By modeling the force ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 614.62pt, "analysis of LMCs, we found that the key to the LMC motion regulation by electric field ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 630.22pt, "lies in the pressure difference caused by the surface tension gradient generated across ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 645.82pt, "the liquid metal nucleus. The magnitude of this force is closely related to the structural ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 661.42pt, "ratio between the solution and the liquid metal nucleus within the hydrogel membrane. ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 677.02pt, "Mechanical modeling demonstrates that in the scale range of liquid metal cells that we ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 692.62pt, "have explored, the increase in the proportion of liquid metal nuclei has a significant ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 708.22pt, "gain effect on enhancing the driving force generated by the cell subjected to the electric ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 723.82pt, "field. In addition, comparative experiments with blank groups confirm that pure ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 739.44pt, "solution vesicles without added liquid metal nuclei cannot be driven by electric fields. ")
]

